  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA (descriptive, verb-disciplined) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>CENTCOM confirmed late on September 8 that five Iranian crude oil tankers had been destroyed in a coordinated operation: M/T Kaviz, M/T Charminar, M/T Horizon 1, and M/T Riesco in the Oman Sea, and M/T Derya near Kharg Island. CENTCOM cited two consecutive days of IRGC attempts to shoot down a US warship as the immediate grounds for the operation. The two-day relative lull of September 6–7 (Day 191–192) ended with the single heaviest tanker destruction operation of the conflict to date, with direct consequences for commercial transit through the strait. → moved <span class="cite">F4</span></p>
      <p>IRGC answered the tanker destruction on September 8 with a salvo of 20 ballistic missiles targeting Al Azraq air base in Jordan. Jordan's armed forces reported 18 intercepted; two fell in uninhabited desert without reported casualties. Brent crude traded to $100.29 intraday on September 9 — the first triple-digit intraday print since mid-July — with an end-of-day settlement of $97.89 for the eighth as the base level. The kinetic exchange in the 24-hour window of September 8–9 was bilateral and symmetrical in structure, though not in scale. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
      <p>Iran's Foreign Minister Araghchi issued a statement on September 9 explicitly establishing that "the possibility of resuming negotiations does not exist" until the United States "compensates for what it violated" under the June MOU. The Oman channel has remained suspended since August 18. Qatar's characterisation of "very progressive stages" in indirect talks, used on August 4, has not been cited by any party in the past 48 hours. → moved <span class="cite">F3</span></p>
      <p>The Strait of Hormuz recorded approximately six commercial vessel transits per day (7-day rolling average per September 7 data) against a pre-crisis baseline of approximately 85 vessels per day. Iran's Persian Gulf Exclusion Zone designating 57 blacklisted vessels remained active and unmodified. At the Fujairah anchorage, 32 of 165 anchored vessels were running dark with 22 carrying Iran-linked risk designations — this represents offshore transshipment activity rather than Hormuz transits. No official authority decision on channel opening or blacklist modification was reported in the past 48 hours. → supports <span class="cite">F4</span> without move</p>
      <p>The Jerusalem Post published a poll (field dates approximately September 5–7) showing Likud projected at 24 mandates against Eisenkot's Yashar at 23 — a position in which Likud has retaken the marginal lead it lost during a period in mid-August when Yashar was level or +1 in several surveys. The Kan poll from September 6 shows the reverse: Yashar 23, Likud 20. Coalition arithmetic for Netanyahu's bloc held at 57–59 mandates in both surveys, below the constitutional threshold of 61. No new voter surveys were published in the past 24 hours. → supports <span class="cite">F5</span> without move</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 4. SCENARIO MAP (computed summary) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="scenario-map">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Scenario Map
      <span class="meta">Computed from Forecast Board · 1 sentence per scenario</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="scenario-map">
